sequenceDiagram
  title Login flow — stateless token issuance
    participant C as Client
    participant S as POST /auth/login (FastAPI)
    participant B as Supabase

    C->>S: POST /auth/login (email, password)
    S->>B: sign_in_with_password(email, password)
    B-->>S: 201 Created with {user, access_token, refresh_token, session}
    S-->>C: 201 Created — return user + session (includes access_token)
    Note over C: Client stores `access_token` (Bearer) and `refresh_token` securely
    Note over S: Server does not persist session — verification is stateless via Bearer token
    C->>S: Subsequent requests: `Authorization: Bearer <access_token>`
    S->>B: get_user(access_token) — validate token (stateless)
    B-->>S: valid user
    S-->>C: protected resource response
